4) due to the potential for severe harm or death if left unaddressed. The fact that two independent overnight reviews and cloud-side classifier logs confirm the misses, along with the documented recurrence in separate patients on the same software version, establishes a clear deployed-population impact and necessitates immediate field safety action. While the confirmatory device confidence-score log is missing (ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2025A, ARTIFACT-TESTLOG-2029A), the clinical review stands as definitive evidence of the failure. The incident triggers obligations under EU MDR Annex I, Section 17.1 regarding electronic programmable systems and their reliability, and Section 17.2 concerning software development lifecycle and cybersecurity. Furthermore, it requires compliance with 21 CFR \u00a7 820.10(c) due to the device being automated with computer software.", "recommendation": "ESCALATE_TO_HUMAN_IMMEDIATE", "requires_human_review": true, "severity": 4}, "final_report_sha256": "db5b750816497f4f6c8e006855ec2f56236b8f4af32efe46b540c10923554db0", "generation_source": "ollama_real", "invalid_proposals": 0, "is_fallback": false, "is_mock": false, "opa_actions": ["severity4_or_death_forced_immediate_human_escalation", "technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence", "deny:technical_incident_missing_technical_evidence"], "recommendation": "ESCALATE_TO_HUMAN_IMMEDIATE", "record_type": "terminal", "report_id": "SYN-IND-0026", "retrievals": 1, "revisions": 0, "run_id": "SYN-IND-0026_r5", "scenario_id": "SYN-IND-0026", "schema_version": "2.1.0", "severity": 4, "shacl_findings": [], "state_terminal": "terminal", "termination_reason": "human escalation or invalid transition", "timestamp_utc": "2026-08-04T23:11:45.718061Z", "total_steps": 5, "trace_id": "db939cf9-38e4-4f11-b46c-36ec084e87a6"}
